
Big Picture

We want a DevOps Agent that can:

Answer why something happened (reasoning)

Fetch facts from logs/docs (RAG)

Query live systems (APIs)

Read historical data (DB)

Combine everything into one correct answer

-----------------------------------------------

| Component | Answers                 |
| --------- | ----------------------- |
| RAG       | What should be done     |
| DB        | What happened before    |
| API       | What is happening now   |
| LLM       | Why & what next         |


 This is not chatbot behavior
This is assistant + investigator + operator behavior

 What is RAG in Simple Terms in Devops context
Without RAG

LLM guesses based on training data

With RAG

LLM answers only after reading your real data

DevOps RAG examples

Runbooks

SOPs

Past incidents

Terraform docs

Architecture diagrams

Postmortems

RAG = “Search first, answer later”

 What is DB in this Architecture
DB is for structured, historical, factual data

Typical DevOps DB data

Incident history

Deployment records

Cost tables

Metrics snapshots

SLA violations

Example questions answered by DB

“How many times did this service fail last month?”

“Was this error seen before?”

“Which deploy caused the highest error rate?”

 DB = facts over time

 What are APIs in this Architecture

APIs give real-time system state

DevOps APIs

Cloud Run API → service status

Cloud Logging API → recent logs

Monitoring API → CPU/memory

GitHub API → commits & PRs

Kubernetes API → pod restarts

Example questions answered by APIs

“Is the service down right now?”

“What changed in the last 10 minutes?”

“Is autoscaling active?”

APIs = live truth
